## What to do
1. Reproduce ZoneWorld ×3 keeping logs; correlate the seal, the peer transport blip (why did zn-ea93 go to Connecting? autoconnect handover `zone-node-1.log:17319`?) and the
   Hello resend during drain.
2. Root-cause at the owner: which component re-issues Hello after `admission_sealed` (auto-connect expectation re-arm on DISCONNECTED? peer state machine retry?) and why the
   drain waits on it. Per §14 the sealed node performs no new admissions; peer loss during drain is handled by the drain (Draining publication, no re-admission). One rule,
   no new timer/flag if the seal state already exists — route the re-admission trigger through the existing seal check.
3. Regression: unit test — sealed mesh node receives DISCONNECTED/expectation change → no Hello; drain completes within the deadline. Then ZoneWorld ×3 (exit 0, all verdicts),
   `bash samples/run_samples.sh` once, unit half `--filter 'FullyQualifiedName!~CanonicalActorJoinIngressReplyTests'` once.

